tinker kitchen is for anybody who likes  to cook who want to be able to do stuff  that they can't do at home we're almost  like a real-life version of the Iron  Chef set but with a community that  explores food and cooking together this  great big story is brought to you by  Delta when we venture out into the world  we see all that we share my name is Dan  Mills and I'm the founder of tinker  kitchen relaunched in October of 2018  we're a maker space where people can  come together to cook for fun or to  prototype ideas for new food products  before I had tinker kitchen I was  collecting kitchen equipment at home my  wife was very supportive and she allowed  me to expand the kitchen into the living  room but then I realized that I actually  wanted more kitchen equipment that I  could fit the idea came to us to open a  kitchen space that anybody could come to  and then we could share all of the  kitchen equipment and we could get even  bigger and better things  tinker kitchen is kind of like a gym in  that we're a space that has a lot of  machines that once you become a member  of the space you can come and you can  use for whatever you like maybe they  want to use freeze dryer to freeze dry  some food or maybe they want to use deep  fryer to fry some food maybe they want  to make chocolate from being the bar or  a dehydrator or making fruit leathers or  chips what else oh we have we have a  grain mill so we've had people who come  here to build their own flour and then  make bread and they have a very nice  blowtorch with a series of attachment  that you can use to sear just about  anything and sometimes I use it to make  myself a real tea sandwich I like to  cook everything like I'd love to extrude  pasta but I also like other very sciency  things for example making ice cream with  liquid nitrogen  it tickles my nerdy roots I love to be  here when there are other people around  making cool things sometimes I'm the  beneficiary from being able to taste  things that people make one thing that  was surprising is just how many people  there are that are interested in in  cooking and cooking together even with  people that they didn't know beforehand  I feel like I've found my tribe these  are people who understand my nerdy  impulses to like really understand the  science of food so that's pretty  exciting to find people who are just  like me  [Music]
 

